      "title": "RAII and the new/delete Problem",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "RAII and the new/delete Problem",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What RAII Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RAII==: acquire in the **constructor**, release in the **destructor**",
                "Destructor runs on ==every scope exit==: return, early return, exception"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Constructor",
                    "sub": "acquire",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Use",
                    "sub": "may throw or return early",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Destructor",
                    "sub": "release, always",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Why Raw new/delete Fails",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto p = new T;",
                "f();        // throws -> delete skipped",
                "delete p;"
              ],
              "note": "leaks on exception or early return"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Allocate",
                "Release",
                "Wrong (UB)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`new T`",
                  "`delete p`",
                  "`delete[] p`, `free(p)`"
                ],
                [
                  "`new T[n]`",
                  "`delete[] p`",
                  "`delete p`"
                ],
                [
                  "`malloc`",
                  "`free(p)`",
                  "`delete p`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Double delete== and **use-after-free** are UB",
                "`p = nullptr` after delete is a band-aid, not ownership"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The Rule",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:No naked} `new`/`delete` in application code",
                "Raw `T*` or `T&` = ==non-owning observer==",
                "Ownership lives in a **RAII type**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "If cleanup is written by hand after a call that can throw, it is a ==leak waiting to happen==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "unique_ptr: Exclusive Ownership",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "unique_ptr: Exclusive Ownership",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What unique_ptr Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::unique_ptr<T>` ==owns one object== exclusively",
                "Default deleter: {green:zero overhead} vs a raw pointer",
                "Destructor runs ==delete== automatically on scope exit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Not copyable}, only ==movable==",
                "`auto b = std::move(a);` leaves `a` **null**",
                "`unique_ptr<T[]>` uses `delete[]` and supports `p[i]`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Access API",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Effect",
                "Deletes?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`get()`",
                  "borrow the raw pointer",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`release()`",
                  "give up ownership, return pointer",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "`reset(p)`",
                  "delete old object, take `p`",
                  "{red:old one}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto a = std::make_unique<int>(7);",
                "auto b = std::move(a);   // a is now null",
                "int* raw = b.release();  // you must delete raw",
                "delete raw;"
              ],
              "note": "release() hands the delete duty back to you"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Passing and Returning",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Intent",
                "Parameter / return"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Transfer ownership",
                  "`f(std::unique_ptr<T> p)` by value"
                ],
                [
                  "Merely use it",
                  "`f(T* p)` or `f(T& r)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Factory result",
                  "return by value, ==moves automatically=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never `delete` a pointer from `get()`, and never build a second owner from it. `release()` is the only way to hand ownership out."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "shared_ptr, weak_ptr and make_shared",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "shared_ptr, weak_ptr and make_shared",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Control Block",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Holds {blue:strong count}, {purple:weak count}, ==deleter==",
                "Strong count hits ==0== → object destroyed",
                "Copy bumps count **atomically**",
                "Control block thread-safe; ==pointee is not=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cycles and weak_ptr",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "A owns B",
                    "sub": "shared_ptr",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "B owns A",
                    "sub": "shared_ptr",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Never 0",
                    "sub": "leak",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fix",
                    "sub": "weak_ptr back-ref",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==weak_ptr== does not keep the object alive",
                "`lock()` gives a shared_ptr, or null if expired",
                "`expired()` checks"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::weak_ptr<Node> wp = sp;",
                "if (auto s = wp.lock()) {",
                "    use(*s);  // alive here",
                "}",
                "bool gone = wp.expired();"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. One Control Block",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`shared_ptr<T> a(p), b(p);` → two control blocks",
                "Both delete `p` → ==double delete==",
                "In a class, use `shared_from_this()`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "struct W : std::enable_shared_from_this<W> {",
                "    std::shared_ptr<W> self() {",
                "        return shared_from_this();",
                "    }",
                "};"
              ],
              "note": "object must already be owned by a shared_ptr"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why do cycles leak?** Strong counts never reach 0.",
                "**Is shared_ptr thread-safe?** Control block yes, pointee no.",
                "**Why not shared_ptr(this)?** It makes a second control block."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
