    {
      "title": "make_unique and make_shared",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "make_unique and make_shared",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Prefer make_* over new",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==`std::make_unique<T>(args)`== and ==`std::make_shared<T>(args)`== replace `new`",
                "Type is named **once**: `auto p = std::make_unique<Foo>(1);`",
                "{green:Exception safe} in argument lists: no leak if another argument throws"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. make_shared: one allocation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Allocations",
                "Cache"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`make_shared<T>()`",
                  "**1** (object + control block)",
                  "{green:friendly}"
                ],
                [
                  "`shared_ptr<T>(new T)`",
                  "**2** (object, then block)",
                  "{red:scattered}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Trade-off: object and block share one chunk",
                "Object is destroyed at strong count 0, but its ==memory stays== until the last `weak_ptr` dies"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits and the default",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "make_* cannot take a ==custom deleter== or a ==brace-init list==",
                "Fall back to the constructor with `new`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::shared_ptr<FILE> f(fopen(\"a.txt\", \"r\"), fclose);",
                "std::unique_ptr<std::vector<int>> v(new std::vector<int>{1, 2});",
                "auto u = std::make_unique<Foo>();",
                "std::shared_ptr<Foo> s = std::move(u);"
              ],
              "note": "lines 1-2: constructor fallbacks; lines 3-4: unique to shared"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default to unique_ptr",
              "text": "Start with ==unique_ptr==. Convert to `shared_ptr` only when ownership is **truly shared**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Move Semantics, Rvalue References and Copy Elision",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Move Semantics, Rvalue References and Copy Elision",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lvalue, Rvalue, std::move",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:lvalue} = has a name and an address; {blue:rvalue} = temporary",
                "`T&&` binds to temporaries, so it can ==steal resources==",
                "`std::move(x)` is only a ==cast to `T&&`==; the move constructor does the transfer",
                "Moved-from object: ==valid but unspecified==; only destroy or assign to it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Writing a Move",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Steal the pointer, ==null the source==, mark it ==noexcept==",
                "Without `noexcept`, `std::vector` ==copies== on reallocation"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "Widget(Widget&& o) noexcept",
                "    : p(o.p) { o.p = nullptr; }",
                "Widget b = std::move(a);  // a.p is null"
              ],
              "note": "a is still valid, just empty"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Return, Forward, Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Return form",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`return local;`",
                  "{green:elided or moved}"
                ],
                [
                  "`return std::move(local);`",
                  "{red:blocks RVO}"
                ],
                [
                  "`return T{};`",
                  "{green:elision guaranteed (C++17)}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A named `T&&` parameter is an ==lvalue== inside the function",
                "Forward with `std::forward<T>` in templates, else `std::move`",
                "==Rule of zero==: hold smart pointers or containers, write no special members",
                "Define one of the five? ==Consider all== (rule of five)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`std::move` moves nothing, and never read a moved-from object."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
