      "title": "Smart Pointers and Move Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Smart Pointers and Move Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who owns it?",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Sole owner",
                  "==unique_ptr=="
                ],
                [
                  "Shared owner",
                  "==shared_ptr=="
                ],
                [
                  "Observe shared, no ownership",
                  "==weak_ptr=="
                ],
                [
                  "Non-owning use",
                  "`T*` / `T&`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create, transfer, check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "auto u = std::make_unique<T>(1);",
                "auto s = std::make_shared<T>(1);",
                "auto u2 = std::move(u);  // u is null",
                "std::weak_ptr<T> w = s;",
                "if (auto p = w.lock()) { }  // null if expired"
              ],
              "note": "check a smart pointer with if (s)"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "unique_ptr",
                "shared_ptr"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`get()` borrows",
                  "`get()` borrows"
                ],
                [
                  "`release()` gives up, no delete",
                  "`use_count()` strong count"
                ],
                [
                  "`reset(p)` deletes old, takes p",
                  "`reset()` drops one share"
                ],
                [
                  "`swap(o)`",
                  "`lock()` via weak_ptr"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Move rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::move` is a ==cast== to `T&&`; it moves nothing",
                "Moved-from is ==valid but unspecified==: destroy or assign only",
                "Mark moves ==noexcept==, or vector copies on growth",
                "Never `return std::move(local)`: it blocks elision"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Top pitfalls",
